    "All content is read through connected GitHub tools at the pinned source checkpoint; no local repository source is used.",
    "This scope contains 202 tracked text files, all Markdown, across numbered roots 00-10 excluding FEIS root 08. Earlier unledgered reading is not counted.",
    "The top-level historical master index includes dated counts and observations that must not be treated as live inventory; its 2026-09-30 addendum labels new proposals as additions, not approved replacements.",
    "NEX-STD-006 Knowledge Governance Framework explicitly has Draft status despite constitutional framing; Approved documents and historical index prose reference it. Presence is not approval. Approved NEX-STD-002/-003/-004/-005 have blank effective and review dates.",
    "Identity Model is currently NEX-STD-123 v1.0.1, with explicit 2026-08-29 reassignment; old collision warnings preserved elsewhere are historical. USER.md asserts Professional Mechanical Engineer (PME), which must be reconciled with verified credentials before external professional use.",
    "Architecture Compiler Protocol is Active Operating Instruction effective 2026-10-06 with sequential 2026-10-11 clarifications. Current Compiler–Builder–Auditor Contract supersedes Astra-specific selection wording, requires actual identities and independent top-tier audit before accepted coding package. CFO/CMO/customer-service profiles are design-only Draft, uncommissioned.",
    "Knowledge Management standards preserve review vs approval separation, require approval before baseline adoption, and emphasize reusable conclusions rather than raw conversation. Several Related Documents labels misassign Document Control to NEX-STD-001 and Decision Evolution to NEX-STD-002; actual governance files are NEX-STD-002 and NEX-STD-003.",
    "Canonical Truth Resolution Standard remains Proposed; enterprise architecture reconciliation remains Proposed; cross-system relationship map has working/pending global status plus specifically labeled approved and later scoped extensions. In root 05, KNOWLEDGE_PRESERVATION_STANDARD.md contains only a breadcrumb; root 04 holds the substantive Approved NEX-STD-023.",
    "NEX-STD-124 through 128 and Sep 27 evolution ADR are Approved, distinct 16 enterprise functions with single accountable outcome owners. Very Strong expressly concerns organizational knowledge architecture, not staffing, deployed software, legal registration or operating control effectiveness. Enterprise role, record owner, approver, executor and independent auditor remain distinct.",
    "NEX-STD-052 and 056 use an Advisory-to-Optimization 0-4 agent-level taxonomy differing from foundational NEX-STD-013 Observe-to-Autonomous 0-5. Do not equate numeric levels across documents. Capability registry NEX-PREOS-004 is Proposed; registration is not execution authorization.",
    "Oct 15 Adaptive Reasoning NEX-STD-092 is Approved and the 12-case pack is Approved Capability Validation Pack; the controlled log explicitly leaves numeric maturity NOT_BASELINED. These define measurable behaviors, not demonstrated live runtime capability or model training.",
    "NEX-STD-096 uses Reference-to-Autonomous Optimization levels 0-4, another distinct authority taxonomy; its wording is not directly interchangeable with NEX-STD-013 or NEX-STD-052/056. NEX-STD-091 daily rhythm has an Oct 15 capability practice addendum requiring meaningful evidence rather than routine capability-log noise.",
    "NEX-STD-116 has an Oct 9 work-management extension: planning defects, waiting materials, failed tests, reopened orders and tool/access constraints are reliability signals, expressly not substitutes for physical failure evidence. NEX-STD-097/-119 distinguish operational data ownership and future integration; approved architecture does not prove live platform integration. NEX-STD-087/-099 define activation/release gates; document existence alone is insufficient.",
    "NEX-STD-088/-090 prescribe a recommended older numbered repository layout with 04_Projects and NEX-STD-111 recommends Obsidian/local/cloud backup with Git described as future. Those text recommendations differ from the actual GitHub tree and the user's explicit GitHub-only Projects/Active policy; preserve as historical architectural reference, do not create local vaults or reorganize current repository from them. NEX-STD-047 Related Documents has stale IDs (e.g. Constitution as NEX-STD-003), so use verified file paths."
